+# Solution
+
+`sheet/engine.py` uses a recursive-descent parser for formulas and a memoized
+resolver for cell dependencies.
+
+The parser implements the documented precedence and associativity rules,
+including right-associative exponentiation and unary minus binding less tightly
+than `^`. It also handles parentheses, insignificant whitespace, decimal
+numbers, and cell references.
+
+Cell values are resolved lazily, so forward and transitive references work.
+Computed values are cached as floats. A set plus the active resolution path
+tracks cells currently being evaluated; revisiting one raises `CycleError` for
+both direct and indirect cycles. Native arithmetic behavior is preserved,
+including `ZeroDivisionError` for division by zero.
